==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|non|is}} ''[[vǫllr]]'', from Germanic ''*walþuz''. Cognate with Faroese {{term|vøllur|lang=fo}}, Norwegian {{term|voll|lang=no}}, Old English {{term|weald}} (English {{term|weald|lang=en}}, {{term|wold|lang=en}}) and Old High German {{term|wald}} (German {{term|Wald}})

===Noun===
